@namespace Beastborne.UI.Components
@using System;
@using System.Collections.Generic;
@using Sandbox;
@using Sandbox.UI;
@using Beastborne.UI;
@using Beastborne.UI.Primitives;
@using Beastborne.Systems;
@inherits Panel

@*
    PhoneLauncher v3 — the PawPad, running TamerLink OS (player-facing
    branding only; code identity stays PhoneLauncher). The phone-shaped
    navigation launcher (Fable 5 sweep, guiding-star §Navigation).
    Summoned by the MENU button / Slot8; the persistent bottom bar stays
    mounted for now (A/B trial — retirement comes after the user blesses
    the phone).

    v4 (live screenshot feedback — "sell the DEVICE"):
    - HIGHLIGHT BARS REMOVED (user dislikes) — the gold→violet energy
      hairline is deleted and the header's gold accent rule is switched
      off (AccentWidth 0 in markup + display:none in our scss — a 0-width
      div can still render as an artifact; empty-div quirk). The title
      breathes on its own.
    - REAL BEZEL — .pl-shell wraps the screen: near-black frame (r-38
      outer / screen keeps r-30; 10px sides, 20px top strip, 12px chin),
      speaker slit + camera lens centered in the top strip, two side-
      button nubs on the LEFT (receding) edge. Footprint 576px wide incl.
      bezel — every doctrine width recomputed: screen content 512, tiles
      160, gaps 16 (rows sum 512 exactly). Shadow/lean/entrance unchanged.
    - LABELS RE-CENTERED, v4.1 FINAL (v4's main-axis-width theory was
      DISPROVEN live: the 160px/392px boxes held, yet the text still drew
      left — text-align is a NO-OP under the leaned ancestor, because the
      transform poisons derived width resolution and the Label's inner
      text box collapses to content width; nothing to align within).
      Fix: centering BY CONSTRUCTION — auto-width spans + razor-computed
      margin-left (LabelPadPx/NamePadPx, calibrated glyph estimates).
      Doctrine: inside a transformed subtree, only explicit px layout
      exists; text-align does not.
    - AVATAR (screenshot: no circle) — the command bar's cb-avatar recipe
      copied VERBATIM (fallback emoji span + absolute 50%+negative-half-
      margin img — cb's comment says flex-centering shifts images), then
      cosmetics adapted to a 22px circle with a 2px violet rim. One-shot
      [pawpad] log of the resolved src fires on first visible frame so
      the next session can diagnose from the log if it's STILL missing.
    - HINTS REBUILT (screenshot: WASD wrapped to "WA/SD"; ENTER cap an
      empty gold blob) — the caps were sized under their text (32px for
      4 chars) with auto-width spans centered by justify-content (zero-
      width anchor under the lean). Every cap AND its inner span now
      carry explicit widths + white-space: nowrap; ENTER's dark GoldInk
      on gold verified in the scss.
    - FPS FIX (live: 7fps open / 43-87 closed) — the ring's per-frame
      ink-lean wave (`Style.Transform` write EVERY frame on an element
      INSIDE the perspective-leaned device) re-dirtied the whole leaned
      subtree each frame and forced a full 3D re-composite. THE WAVE IS
      RETIRED on the PawPad (the menu keeps its waving cursor at ROOT
      level, outside its tilted panels — that's why it's cheap there).
      Ring rect math is now EVENT-DRIVEN (_ringDirty on open/focus move,
      not per-frame), and ClockText is cached (refreshed ≤1/s) so
      BuildHash isn't allocating a DateTime string per frame. Target:
      zero measurable per-frame work while open and idle.
    - ANCHOR HARDENED (live: only a ~40px sliver at the right edge) —
      the root placed the AUTO-width .pl-wrap with justify-content:
      flex-end — the doctrine's zero-width-anchor pattern at the one
      scope it hadn't been applied to. .pl-wrap and .pl-device now carry
      explicit width 576px so flex-end sums a real number. (The sliver
      was possibly also mid-edit hotload — the shell div briefly existed
      with no scss — but the explicit widths make the anchor lawful
      either way.)

    v3.1 (live-test feedback + "make it actually look good" pass):
    - SWEEP BUG ROOT-CAUSED — log-proven: every MAIN APP took the widget
      branch ("[sweepdbg] widget launch 'beasts'"). The record flag was
      renamed Liquid→Sweep in v2, and s&box hotload migrates STATIC data
      across recompiles by copying record members BY NAME — no name match,
      so every migrated PhoneApp got Sweep=default(false), and every later
      hotload faithfully copied the stale false forward. Fix: destination
      vs widget is now classified IN CODE (IsWidgetApp — method bodies are
      always fresh after hotload; only DATA can go stale). The Sweep field
      is deleted so nothing misleading remains. ⚠ Never rename fields in
      the PhoneApp record without expecting a full-restart requirement.
    - RIGHT-SIDE ANCHOR — the phone lives at the right edge (72px in,
      vertically centered) so the game stays visible; entrance is a
      slide-in from the right edge, exit mirrors. Backdrop dim lightened
      to 0.55 — seeing the game behind is now the point.
    - THE LEAN FLIPPED — perspective(1600px) rotateY(-13deg), origin
      right center (the PawPad mockup's values): right side toward the
      camera, left recedes, sold by a left-edge shade overlay + the
      energy hairline along the top edge (device is "on").
    - FOCUS POP — the focused icon lifts toward the player
      (translateY(-4px) scale(1.06), 0.12s) and the living ring RIDES the
      lift: Box.Rect doesn't move with CSS transforms, so UpdateRing
      mirrors the pop into the ring's target rect (the menu's SelectedPop
      lockstep). Press settles back down to scale(0.98) inside the ring.
    - HEADER v2 — PROTOTYPE stamp deleted; status row gains signal bars;
      TAMERLINK OS eyebrow in violet over a 34px italic PawPad with the
      gold accent rule (BbSectionHeader, KickerColor override); Steam
      avatar (command-bar house pattern) beside the tamer line.
    - DOCTRINE TIGHTENED (live: EXPEDITION's label row overran its tile
      and clipped the body edge) — justify-content placement of AUTO-width
      children drifts too, not just space-between/align-items. Labels are
      now single full-width text-align: center spans; keycaps ride the
      icon corner as fixed absolutes; the hints/status rows give every
      child an explicit width. Full strict doctrine in the SCSS header.

    v3 (live-test feedback):
    - THE LIVING RING — the per-tile static rings are dead; ONE violet
      cursor ring (the main menu's signature) glides between focused
      icons on the 0.27s signature ease, with the ink-lean wave running
      per-frame (menu's multi-sine at 60% amplitude). It lives INSIDE
      .pl-grid, so it shares the device's 3D lean with the icons —
      flat Box.Rect delta math positions it, no perspective compensation
      needed (unlike MainMenu's tilted-panel cursor). Snaps on open
      (warmup frames), glides thereafter.
    - ALIGNMENT HARDENED — v2 drifted right in-engine: auto-width flex
      children placed by align-items/space-between landed as if their
      width were zero (labels started at the icon's center and ran right;
      the stamp/LV line ran off the body edge). Fix: every centered or
      right-anchored box now has an EXPLICIT width; centering is done by
      justify-content inside fixed boxes or hard margins, never by
      cross-axis auto placement. Absolute badges get explicit widths
      (width:auto never shrink-wraps an absolute element — quirk).
    - SWEEP_DEBUG — temp per-phase Log.Info proving the accent swipe
      runs (SWAP_DEBUG precedent). Flip false once verified live.

    The phone is a ROUTER, not content: a 3×4 grid of "app" icons, one per
    destination. v2 (live feedback): apps look like APPS — each is an 88px
    rounded square FILLED SOLID with its accent color (the color IS the
    icon; the launcher grid is the one sanctioned full-rainbow surface),
    glyph centered, label below. Tapping an app plays THE ACCENT SWIPE:
    a full-screen angled slab in the app's accent sweeps across the screen
    (the menu→game Persona-wipe vocabulary, single accent, phone-speed),
    NavManager routes at full cover, the slab sweeps off the far side.

    Juice-tier discipline: the swipe plays for DESTINATIONS (the 6 tabs +
    Quests + Bag — full-screen contexts). The four widget apps
    (Chat/Radio/Effects/Notifications) just close the phone and toggle
    their popup — a fullscreen accent sweep to open a chat widget would
    be Tier-4 juice on a Tier-1 action.

    Engine rules honored (css-quirks.md):
    - Root PARKS OFFSCREEN when closed (left -10000px, never display-flip).
    - Backdrop uses top/left + width/height 100% — all-edge absolute
      stretching resolves to ZERO SIZE on an empty element.
    - 3D lean holder (.pl-device) carries NO bg/border — the painted
      device lives on a direct child (.pl-shell, screen inside it).
    - Swipe slab = solid div; position/size/translate/skew are IMPERATIVE
      per-frame Style writes (class-toggle transforms snap; per-frame
      re-assert survives any mid-cover rebuild — the held-tween lesson).
    - Slab geometry converts Box.Rect screen px → style px via
      ScaleFromScreen (+30% oversize) so cover is guaranteed at any
      window scale (the liquid circle under-covered without this).
    - Icon children are pointer-events: none (hover-flicker rule).

    Keyboard (registered with UIModalState as "PhoneLauncher"):
    WASD walk the grid · Enter/Space launch · number keys + T/R/C/N route
    directly to their app · Q/Esc/Slot8 close. Hover == focus (one cursor).
*@

<root class="phone-root @(Shown ? "shown" : "") @(IsVisible ? "open" : "") @(_fx != FxPhase.Idle ? "fx-live" : "")">
    <div class="pl-backdrop" onclick=@OnBackdropClicked></div>

    <div class="pl-wrap">
        <div class="pl-device" @ref="_deviceRef">

            <!-- THE SHELL — the physical device: near-black bezel frame,
                 r-38 outer. Speaker slit + camera lens live in the top
                 strip; the old surface becomes the SCREEN inside (r-30).
                 The shell is a CHILD of the transform holder, so its
                 bg/shadow project correctly with the 3D lean (only the
                 holder's OWN fills render flat — quirk). -->
            <div class="pl-shell">
                <div class="pl-bezel-top">
                    <div class="pl-speaker"></div>
                    <div class="pl-camera"><div class="pl-camera-lens"></div></div>
                </div>

                <div class="pl-surface" @ref="_surfaceRef">
                <!-- v7.2: the LOOPING wallpaper (spec animations, retimed to
                     a seamless 16s master loop, baked to animated WebP) —
                     an absolute img so the texture animates; the surface
                     paints no fill of its own. Geometry is FIXED (v7.3):
                     surface height is deterministic, the img is the bake
                     size 1:1 — runtime measuring stretched the texture and
                     squared off the corner curves (user report). -->
                <img class="pl-wall" src="ui/pawpad/wallpaper.webp" />
                <!-- v7 "3a Graphite" status row (design handoff spec): clock
                     left; right group = GOLD signal bars · battery · divider
                     · name · gold-ringed avatar. NO title header anymore —
                     the spec's screen is status → grid → dock; the paw brand
                     lives on the chin deboss. Right group is right-anchored
                     BY CONSTRUCTION (computed margin — the only alignment
                     primitive under the lean); every box explicit px. -->
                <div class="pl-top">
                    <span class="pl-clock">@ClockText</span>
                    <div class="pl-right">
                        <div class="pl-sig" style="margin-left: @(RightPadPx())px;">
                            <div class="pl-sig-bar b1"></div>
                            <div class="pl-sig-bar b2"></div>
                            <div class="pl-sig-bar b3"></div>
                            <div class="pl-sig-bar b4"></div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="pl-batt">
                            <div class="pl-batt-body"><div class="pl-batt-fill"></div></div>
                            <div class="pl-batt-nub"></div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="pl-divider"></div>
                        <span class="pl-lv">@TamerLine</span>
                        <!-- Guild-recipe avatar (plain in-flow img, explicit
                             px — 50% offsets die under the lean). Spec: 24px
                             circle, 2px GOLD ring. -->
                        @if ( GetSteamId() > 0 )
                        {
                            <img class="pl-ava-steam" src="avatar:@GetSteamId()" />
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <img class="pl-ava-steam" src="@GetAvatarImagePath()" />
                        }
                    </div>
                </div>

                @if ( _appView != null )
                {
                    <!-- ═══ IN-PHONE APP (TamerLink OS, v9 — user call: chat/
                         radio/effects/alerts LIVE ON the phone, not popups).
                         Mouse goes through the backdrop router: every
                         clickable carries `pl-hit hit-<action>` and
                         ActionAtScreen inverse-projects the cursor onto it.
                         Q backs out to the home grid. -->
                    <div class="pl-appview" @ref="_appviewRef">
                        <div class="pl-av-head">
                            <div class="pl-av-back pl-hit hit-back"><span>&lt;</span></div>
                            <span class="pl-av-title" style="color: @AppViewAccent();">@AppViewTitle()</span>
                        </div>

                        @if ( _appView == "chat" )
                        {
                            <div class="pl-chan-row">
                                <div class="pl-chan pl-hit hit-chan-global @(_phoneChan == "global" ? "on" : "")"><span>GLOBAL</span></div>
                                <div class="pl-chan pl-hit hit-chan-guild @(_phoneChan == "guild" ? "on" : "")"><span>GUILD</span></div>
                                <div class="pl-chan pl-hit hit-chan-trade @(_phoneChan == "trade" ? "on" : "")"><span>TRADE</span></div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="pl-chat-scroll" @ref="_chatScrollRef">
                                @foreach ( var m in PhoneMessages() )
                                {
                                    <div class="pl-msg @(IsOwnPhoneMsg( m ) ? "own" : "")">
                                        <span class="pl-msg-author">@m.PlayerName</span>
                                        <span class="pl-msg-text">@m.Content</span>
                                    </div>
                                }
                            </div>
                            <div class="pl-chat-inputrow pl-hit hit-input">
                                <ChatInputBox @ref="_phoneChatBox" OnSubmit=@OnPhoneChatSend />
                                <div class="pl-send pl-hit hit-send"><span>SEND</span></div>
                            </div>
                        }
                        else if ( _appView == "radio" )
                        {
                            <div class="pl-radio-now">
                                <span class="pl-radio-station">@(Beastborne.Systems.RadioManager.CurrentStation?.Name ?? "RADIO")</span>
                                <span class="pl-radio-track">@(Beastborne.Systems.RadioManager.CurrentTrack?.Name ?? "No track")</span>
                            </div>
                            <div class="pl-radio-ctls">
                                <div class="pl-rctl pl-hit hit-radio-prev"><iconify icon="lucide:skip-back" Size=@(22) Color="#f4f1ea" /></div>
                                <div class="pl-rctl big pl-hit hit-radio-play"><iconify icon="@(Beastborne.Systems.RadioManager.IsPlaying ? "lucide:pause" : "lucide:play")" Size=@(28) Color="#2a1605" /></div>
                                <div class="pl-rctl pl-hit hit-radio-next"><iconify icon="lucide:skip-forward" Size=@(22) Color="#f4f1ea" /></div>
                            </div>
                        }
                        else if ( _appView == "effects" )
                        {
                            <div class="pl-list-scroll">
                                @foreach ( var row in ActiveEffectsPanel.GetPhoneRows() )
                                {
                                    <div class="pl-fx-row">
                                        <span class="pl-fx-name">@row.Label</span>
                                        <span class="pl-fx-val">@row.Value</span>
                                    </div>
                                }
                                @if ( ActiveEffectsPanel.GetPhoneRows().Count == 0 )
                                {
                                    <span class="pl-empty">NO ACTIVE EFFECTS</span>
                                }
                            </div>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <div class="pl-list-scroll">
                                @foreach ( var n in PhoneNotifications() )
                                {
                                    <div class="pl-alert-row">
                                        <span class="pl-alert-title">@n.Title</span>
                                        <span class="pl-alert-msg">@n.Message</span>
                                    </div>
                                }
                                @if ( PhoneNotifications().Count == 0 )
                                {
                                    <span class="pl-empty">ALL CAUGHT UP</span>
                                }
                            </div>
                        }
                    </div>
                }
                else
                {
                <div class="pl-grid" @ref="_gridRef">
                    @for ( int r = 0; r < 4; r++ )
                    {
                        <div class="pl-row">
                            @for ( int c = 0; c < 3; c++ )
                            {
                                var i = r * 3 + c;
                                var app = Apps[i];
                                var badge = GetBadgeCount( app.Id );
                                <div class="pl-app @(i == _kb ? "focused" : "")"
                                     onclick=@(() => LaunchIndex( i ))
                                     onmouseover=@(() => HoverTile( i ))>
                                    <div class="pl-app-iconwrap">
                                        <!-- v5.3 (user call): apps are FLAT on the glass at rest —
                                             a phone reads 2D until you pick one up. On focus the
                                             tile lifts 6px and a planted shadow appears beneath it
                                             (y: 5 + FocusPopLift 6 = 11 counters the lift so the
                                             shading sits ON the glass, not on the tile). The rest
                                             value is a ZERO-SIZE shadow, not a removed property —
                                             s&box never clears a removed inline style prop. -->
                                        <!-- v7: NO hover-brighten (user: it messes with the
                                             colors) — the accent stays true; lift + planted
                                             shadow + ring + animated glyph carry the focus. -->
                                        <div class="pl-app-icon" style="background-color: @app.Accent; box-shadow: @(i == _kb ? "5px 9px" : "0px 0px") 0px @(Darken( app.Accent ));">
                                            <!-- v5: the commissioned icon set (Claude Design,
                                                 icons/v2) — filled-silhouette SVGs that carry
                                                 their own fill color (white; dark ink baked in
                                                 for shop/effects), so DarkGlyph stays data-only.
                                                 The PhoneApp.Icon lucide id is retired but the
                                                 FIELD stays: hotload migrates static records BY
                                                 NAME and shape changes force restarts.
                                                 v6: focus swaps the SRC to the looping animated
                                                 WebP (attribute VALUE swap — the diff-safe path;
                                                 an if-branch icon swap leaves ghost children.
                                                 NOTE: razor parses at-directives INSIDE html
                                                 comments — never write at-if in a comment). -->
                                            <img class="pl-app-glyph" src="@GlyphSrc( i, app.Id )" />
                                        </div>
                                        <!-- v5.1: corner keycaps REMOVED (user: "just in the
                                             way"). The hotkeys still WORK — they're just not
                                             printed on every tile anymore. -->
                                        @if ( app.Id == "bag" && HasNewItems() )
                                        {
                                            <BbStamp Text="NEW" Tone="gold" Tilt=@(3) Class="pl-new-stamp" />
                                        }
                                        else if ( badge > 0 )
                                        {
                                            <span class="pl-badge @(app.DarkGlyph ? "dark-ink" : "")" style="background-color: @app.Accent;">@FormatBadge( badge )</span>
                                        }
                                    </div>
                                    <!-- v4.1: centering BY CONSTRUCTION. Live capture proved
                                         text-align is a no-op anywhere under the lean: the
                                         transformed ancestor poisons derived width resolution
                                         (the documented translate(-50%) flex-poison law), so
                                         the Label's inner text box collapses to content width
                                         and there is nothing to center within — even when the
                                         span's own 160px main-axis box HOLDS (proven by the
                                         avatar landing flush right of .pl-lv's held 392px).
                                         Only explicit px survive in here: auto-width span
                                         (content-collapse now works FOR us) + computed
                                         margin-left. -->
                                    <div class="pl-app-labelrow">
                                        <span class="pl-app-label" style="margin-left: @(LabelPadPx( app.Label ))px;">@app.Label</span>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            }
                        </div>
                    }

                </div>

                <!-- THE SYSTEM DOCK (v5) — meta destinations (Profile /
                     Settings / Guide / Feedback) as a quieter tier below
                     the grid: smaller dark-violet tiles, violet glyphs
                     (system chrome, not apps). No labels — dock convention;
                     the ring + glyphs carry it. Indices 12-15 in the one
                     cursor space. justify-content: center is LEGAL here:
                     every child is an explicit 56px box (doctrine rule 2). -->
                <div class="pl-dock" @ref="_dockRef">
                    @for ( int d = 0; d < Dock.Length; d++ )
                    {
                        var di = GridCount + d;
                        var dockId = Dock[d];
                        <div class="pl-dock-app @(di == _kb ? "focused" : "")"
                             onclick=@(() => LaunchIndex( di ))
                             onmouseover=@(() => HoverTile( di ))>
                            <img class="pl-dock-glyph" src="@GlyphSrc( di, dockId )" />
                        </div>
                    }
                </div>
                }
                </div>

                <!-- v7 chin — the spec's DEBOSSED paw: highlight copy offset
                     1px down under a recess copy (stacked absolute imgs with
                     explicit px inside an unpainted holder — lawful). -->
                <div class="pl-chin">
                    <div class="pl-deboss">
                        <img class="pl-deboss-hi" src="ui/pawpad/paw-deboss-hi.png" />
                        <img class="pl-deboss-lo" src="ui/pawpad/paw-deboss-lo.png" />
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Side-button nubs — RIGHT edge, DOM-AFTER the shell (v7.2:
                 painted OVER the trim; DOM-before let the opaque shell
                 cover their overlap and only a detached sliver showed,
                 user-reported twice). Explicit boxes throughout. -->
            <div class="pl-nub nub-a"></div>
            <div class="pl-nub nub-b"></div>

            <!-- Receding-side shade — a SIBLING of the shell (absolute
                 children paint BEHIND a panel's own background fill —
                 engine quirk — so it must sit beside the painted shell,
                 not inside it). DOM order paints it above; pointer-events
                 none. The v3.1 energy hairline is DELETED (v4 user call). -->
            <div class="pl-shade"></div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- THE LIVING RING — one violet cursor for the whole grid (menu
         signature). v4.2: RELOCATED to ROOT level, OUTSIDE the leaned
         subtree — the menu's own placement, and the fix for BOTH v4
         regressions at once: (1) per-frame wave writes are cheap again
         (they no longer dirty the 3D device — the 7fps law), so the
         liquid ink-lean is BACK; (2) position comes straight from the
         icons' PROJECTED screen rects, so the ring centers exactly on
         every column (the old in-lean delta math assumed uniform scale,
         but perspective compresses the far/left side more — the ring
         drifted sideways on left/middle columns, user-reported).
         left/top/w/h via markup style (CSS transitions glide), wave via
         imperative Style.Transform per frame (never re-renders). -->
    <div @ref="_ringRef" class="pl-cursor @(_ringWarmup >= 2 ? "" : "snap") @(_appView != null ? "hidden" : "")"
         style="left: @(_ringL)px; top: @(_ringT)px; width: @(_ringW)px; height: @(_ringH)px;"></div>

    <!-- THE ACCENT SWIPE slab — solid accent fill, driven entirely
         imperatively from StepFx(). Sits AFTER .pl-wrap so it paints over
         the phone. pointer-events: none — input outruns animation. -->
    <div class="pl-swipe" @ref="_swipe" style="background-color: @_fxAccent;"></div>
</root>

@code {
    // ── Static show/hide API (the house pattern: static IsVisible + BuildHash) ──

    public static PhoneLauncher Instance { get; private set; }

    /// <summary>True while the phone UI is open (UIModalState reads this).</summary>
    public static bool IsVisible { get; private set; }

    // Close animation window — the root stays on-screen (parked-open) until
    // this expires so the reverse transition is visible before parking.
    private static float _closingUntil;

    public static void Show()
    {
        if ( IsVisible ) return;
        IsVisible = true;
        _closingUntil = 0f;
        SoundManager.PlayPopup();
        Instance?.ResetForOpen();
    }

    public static void Close()
    {
        if ( !IsVisible ) return;
        IsVisible = false;
        _closingUntil = Time.Now + 0.18f;
        SoundManager.PlayPopdown();
    }

    public static void Toggle()
    {
        if ( IsVisible ) Close();
        else Show();
    }

    /// <summary>Open the phone directly onto a TamerLink app ("chat",
    /// "radio", "effects", "alerts"). v9.2: the chat POPUP is retired —
    /// T and every chat entry point land here instead.</summary>
    public static void OpenToApp( string id )
    {
        Show();
        if ( Instance != null )
        {
            Instance._appView = id;
            Instance.StateHasChanged();
        }
    }

    // ── App registry — grid order (3 cols × 4 rows) ─────────────────────
    // Each destination owns ONE accent (guiding-star three-color identity:
    // that token drives the icon fill, the badge, and the accent swipe).
    //
    // ⚠ HOTLOAD DATA-STALENESS LAW (learned the hard way): this array is
    // static, and s&box hotload MIGRATES static data across recompiles by
    // copying record members BY NAME — the initializer never re-runs. When
    // v2 renamed the `Liquid` flag to `Sweep`, every live session's
    // migrated PhoneApp got Sweep=default(false) and EVERY destination
    // silently took the widget branch (log-proven: "[sweepdbg] widget
    // launch 'beasts'"). Rules: (1) behavior BRANCHES live in code
    // (IsWidgetApp below), never in migrated data; (2) never rename a
    // field in this record without expecting stale values until a full
    // editor restart.
    private record PhoneApp( string Id, string Label, string Icon, string Accent, string Key, bool IsTab, string RouteId, bool DarkGlyph );

    private static readonly PhoneApp[] Apps =
    {
        // Row 1 — the core loop
        new( "beasts",      "BEASTS",     "lucide:paw-print",      "#7b4ddb", "1", true,  "monsters",   false ),
        new( "skills",      "SKILLS",     "lucide:network",        "#ff6bd6", "2", true,  "skills",     false ),
        new( "expedition",  "EXPEDITION", "lucide:map",            "#ee5421", "3", true,  "expedition", false ),
        // Row 2 — the world
        new( "online",      "ONLINE",     "lucide:globe",          "#3f8fe0", "4", true,  "online",     false ),
